  <definitions>
    <definition term="Fraud Referral" source="Programme glossary G-002">Referral of a claim to the Counter-Fraud &amp; SIU team for investigation.</definition>
    <definition term="Tier-3 Claim" source="Programme glossary G-008">A claim meeting the Tier-3 definition in BR-TRI-003 (v3 from 2025-01-01).</definition>
    <definition term="Fraud Score" source="Programme glossary G-009">Sentinel score from 0 to 100.</definition>
    <definition term="Customer Referral Notice" source="Programme glossary G-021">Written notice to the customer that a claim is subject to additional checks (BR-FRD-032).</definition>
    <definition term="Counter-Fraud &amp; SIU" source="Programme glossary G-012">The Special Investigations Unit (renamed Counter-Fraud &amp; SIU on 2025-09-01).</definition>
    <definition term="BR-FRD-031 v1" source="NISA Circular 2026/04 §3.3; Claims Handling Manual v7.2 §28.3">Refer a claim to SIU when the Sentinel score is 65 or more (all tiers).</definition>
    <definition term="BR-FRD-032 v2" source="NISA Circular 2026/04 §3.2; APPROVED BRD v1.0 (2026-03-12); Claims Handling Manual v7.2 §29.1">Notify the customer in writing within 10 business days of a fraud referral that the claim is subject to additional checks, unless the notice is deferred under BR-FRD-036.</definition>
    <definition term="BR-FRD-033 v1" source="NISA Circular 2026/04 §3.1; Claims Handling Manual v7.2 §28.6">No claim may be declined, reduced or repudiated on the basis of an automated fraud score alone; every adverse outcome requires a documented human review by SIU.</definition>
    <definition term="BR-FRD-034 v1" source="NISA Circular 2026/04 §3.4">Submit the NISA-FR1 fraud referral return within 30 calendar days after each quarter end; first return for Q2 2026 due 2026-07-30.</definition>
    <definition term="BR-FRD-035 v2" source="Claims Handling Manual v7.2 §30.1">SIU must triage a new referral within 3 business days.</definition>
  </definitions>
